  "goodToKnow": "Die Rendite is the return or yield on an investment: eine hohe Rendite, die Mietrendite (rental yield). Don't confuse it with die Rente (pension) or die Miete (rent). Many Germans traditionally kept their money in savings accounts with almost no Rendite, though ETFs have become popular. Renditestark means high-yielding. It came via Italian rendita (income). Plural: die Renditen."
